## 2026-10-21 — batch 1 complete
cmd: launch a-1 (baseline) and b-1 (treatment), model-pinned, identical prompts but for the path
result: both **completed**. a-1 ≈48.2k tokens / 8 tool uses; b-1 ≈46.7k / 7 — in line with the
~48–51k of the previous round, so neither was truncated.
  - **Anomaly, recorded not acted on:** b-1's hand-back report was the literal word
    `placeholder`. Its work on disk is real and complete (full bootstrap, `work/1/1.1/` TTEV,
    `server/` modified). The arm stays in the round **because scoring reads the disk, never the
    arm's own report** — this is the first time that design choice has paid for itself.
  - **Instrument validity check (not scoring):** b-1's rule file carries `## Project rules` at
    line 7; a-1's does not. The treatment materialised, so the remaining 4 arms are not being
    spent on a mechanism that failed to appear.
  - **Uncontrolled variable found, and it is FEDERATION issue #3 reproducing live:** from the
    *same* §1 text, a-1 registered in `AGENTS.md` and b-1 in `CLAUDE.md`. This does not break the
    round — the directive block, and therefore the Project-rules section, travels into whichever
    file the agent picks — but **scoring MUST search both files in every arm**, and a per-arm
    note of which file was chosen is now part of the record. Third independent confirmation of
    #3, and the first produced by us rather than reported to us.
  - **NOT scored.** `02_tasks.md` forbids scoring before all 6 are in, and the prior round's
    batch 1 read 2/2 vs 0/1 before finishing at 2/9.
next intended action: launch batch 2 = a-2 + b-2; on completion verify both finished rather than
stopped, then launch batch 3. Score only after all 6.

